cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "synesis-help: quick reference guide for the Synesis language"
abstract: >
  synesis-help is the offline reference guide of the Synesis ecosystem, in the
  spirit of the Norton Guides: a compiled, instantly searchable, keyboard-driven
  terminal viewer. Diagnostic and field-type entries are derived by probing the
  Synesis compiler itself, so the documentation cannot drift from what the
  compiler does. Licensed under AGPL-3.0-only with the Synesis Data-Output
  Exception; outputs generated by this software are not covered by the AGPL
  (see LICENSE.exception).
authors:
  - family-names: De Britto
    given-names: Christian Maciel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1431-3924"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/synesis-lang/synesis-help"
url: "https://synesis-lang.github.io/synesis-docs"
keywords:
  - qualitative-research
  - documentation
  - reference-guide
  - terminal-user-interface
  - synesis
